# Repo-wide conventions (Sivic Scraper monorepo)

This repo is a monorepo: a Python/FastAPI scraper + dashboard at the root,
plus several independent frontend apps (`city-budget`, `city-budget-simulator`,
`council-accountability`, `crossword-constructor`, `time-timer`,
`meeting-recap`, `apps/problem-frame`) each with their own `package.json`.
Built frontend output is copied into `dashboard/static/<app-name>/` for the
FastAPI app to serve — don't hand-edit files under `dashboard/static/`, they
are build artifacts.

## Scope discipline

- Treat each top-level app directory as its own project. Don't share code
  between apps by reaching across directories; if logic needs to be shared,
  surface that explicitly rather than importing across app boundaries.
- Before adding a new dependency, check whether the specific app (or the root
  `requirements.txt`) already has something that does the job.
- When editing a file, match the conventions already present in that file's
  app/module before applying repo-wide defaults — local consistency wins over
  a global rule.

## Env & secrets

- Config comes from `.env`, loaded via `python-dotenv` (backend) or Vite/Next
  env conventions (frontend). Always add new required variables to the
  corresponding `.env.example` in the same change.
- Never commit real secrets, API keys, or `.env` contents.

## Docs & planning

- Longer-running features get a plan/tracking doc (see `plans/`, `*-PLAN.md`,
  `issues/`) — when asked to implement "as planned", update that doc's status
  (with progress) as steps complete rather than only editing code silently.
- Keep `CHANGELOG.md` and per-app `README.md` files in sync with behavior
  changes that affect how the app is run or deployed.

## Testing before calling work done

- Backend changes: run the relevant `pytest` subset (`pytest.ini` scopes
  `tests/`); skip `e2e`-marked tests only when a live server isn't available.
- Frontend changes: run that app's own `npm run test` / `npm run build` /
  `npm run lint` — each app manages its own scripts, there's no root-level
  aggregate script.
- Don't mark a task complete with failing tests, type errors, or lint errors.

## Git & deployment

- Deployment is via the `deploy-hostinger` GitHub Actions workflow on push to
  `main`/`master` — avoid changes that assume a different deploy target
  without updating `.github/workflows/deploy-hostinger.yml` and
  `docker-compose.yml`/`Dockerfile` together.
- Keep commits scoped to one app/concern where possible, given the monorepo
  has several independently deployable pieces.

## Code style baseline

- Favor small, elegant, well-commented modules over large ones — this matches
  the existing split into per-domain modules (`campaign_finance.py`,
  `council_voting.py`, `police_calls.py`, etc.) rather than a single
  monolithic file per app.
- Match existing naming: snake_case for Python, camelCase for
  JS/TS variables and functions, PascalCase for React components and Python
  classes.
